<title>PORTUGAL: BES bids for rest of BIC shares.</title>
<headline>BES bids for rest of BIC shares.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portugal's Banco Espirito Santo e Comercial de Lisboa (BES), which holds 47 percent of Banco Internacional de Credito, said it was launching a public offer (OPA) to buy the rest of the bank's shares.</p>
<p>In an announcement in the Lisbon bourse's daily bulletin, BES said it was offering 2,790 escudos per share for the 6.12 million shares it does not already hold.</p>
<p>At 0915 GMT BIC's shares were up 285 escudos at 2,585 on volume of just 918.</p>
<p>BIC's share capital is 11.6 billion escudos.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon editorial +(351-1) 3538254</p>
</text>
